<!--
  wp81_notify_alarm - the mark Alarms puts in the status bar.

  The same clock as wp81_glyph_clock, which is the app's own icon, so that a line in the
  shade and the tile it came from are recognisably one program. It is a separate drawable
  only because of the scale: the glyph is drawn to sit inside a tile with air around it,
  which at status-bar size leaves a small clock in the middle of a lot of nothing. Here it
  is enlarged about its own centre to fill the canvas the way a notification icon is meant
  to, without touching the tile's proportions.

  White, with the shape carried entirely by the alpha channel, which is what the system
  needs: a notification icon is re-tinted by the platform and anything that is not
  transparent comes out as a solid block.
-->
